 1  B
 CN + photon = C + N
!
! photoabsorption cross section and photodissociation yield from Leiden database (Heays et al 2017, A&A, 602, A105, https://home.strw.leidenuniv.nl/~ewine/photo/)
!
! photodissociation threshold is 160     nm (Huebner et al 1992) to yield C(3P) + N(4S), although Heays et al (2017) only consider photodissociation to C(3P) + N(2D) with a threshold of 120 nm
! photoionization   threshold is  91.176 nm (Lide, R D, CRC Handbook of Chemistry and Physics, 90th ed, CRC Press 2009), although Heays et al (2017) put it at 87.33 nm
!
! sigma is the total photoabsorption cross section
! yield is the photodissociation yield relative to photoabsorption
!
! wlth[nm]  sigma[cm2]   yield(s)...
